# Generated at runtime. Most of logs/ is local noise, but four things MUST be tracked:
# every GitHub Actions cycle runs on a brand-new runner that checks this repo out fresh, so
# anything not committed does not exist as far as the deployed agent is concerned.
#   audit_log.jsonl      - read by the deployed dashboard (see dashboard/, src/audit_log.py)
#   iv_history_*.csv     - the window iv_rank is measured against. Untracked, every CI cycle
#                          started with zero history, iv_rank came back None, and the
#                          rulebook therefore mandated cash on every single cycle.
#   agent_state.json     - circuit breaker + heartbeat. Untracked, the breaker resets every
#                          15 minutes and can never trip (see src/agent_state.py).
#   archive/             - evidence: the pre-fix audit log containing the observed model
#                          faithfulness failures, and the contaminated IV history.
logs/*
!logs/audit_log.jsonl
!logs/iv_history_*.csv
!logs/agent_state.json
!logs/archive/
!logs/archive/**

# Third-party research PDFs. Cited in README and in the source that implements them, but
# not redistributed here — they are other people's copyrighted work and add ~7MB to a repo
# judges will clone.
*.pdf

